---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
    title="About | 1976 London"
    description="Meet Stuart Hunt, the independent web developer behind 1976 London."
    currentPath="/about"
>
    <section class="page-hero about-hero">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> A little about me</span>
        <h1>Good work starts with <span>a good conversation.</span></h1>
        <p>
            I’m Stuart Hunt, an independent web developer in London. I work
            with artists, photographers, filmmakers, musicians, charities, and
            local businesses to make websites that feel like them and work
            hard for what they do.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-story">
        <div class="about-label">
            <span class="eyebrow">1976 / London</span>
            <p>Independent web development<br />with people at the centre.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-prose">
            <h2>Thoughtful work, without the agency layers.</h2>
            <p>
                1976 London is a small, independent studio. That means you work
                directly with the person shaping and building your site, from
                the first idea through to launch.
            </p>
            <p>
                I build with modern tools like Astro and WordPress, choosing
                the right approach for the project rather than forcing every
                brief into the same shape. The goal is always a clear,
                considered experience that can keep growing with you.
            </p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/work">Take a look at the work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-process">
        <div class="section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> How we work</span>
            <h2>Clear steps.<br /><span>Good collaboration.</span></h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="process-list">
            <li>
                <span class="process-number">01</span>
                <div>
                    <h3>Listen</h3>
                    <p>We start with your work, your audience, and what you want the site to do.</p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="process-number">02</span>
                <div>
                    <h3>Shape</h3>
                    <p>We agree the right structure, content, and direction before building.</p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="process-number">03</span>
                <div>
                    <h3>Build</h3>
                    <p>Your site comes together with care for clarity, accessibility, and performance.</p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="process-number">04</span>
                <div>
                    <h3>Grow</h3>
                    <p>After launch, the site is ready for new work, fresh content, and what comes next.</p>
                </div>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="cta">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> Your turn</span>
        <h2>Tell me what you’re working on.</h2>
        <p>
            A first conversation is a good place to work out what you need and
            whether we’re a good fit.
        </p>
        <div class="button-row">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="/contact">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="/services">See how I can help</a>
        </div>
    </section>
</MainLayout>
